<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Big and Small's giant weapon wielder overlaps Alpha Genes' tough sinews. The B&amp;S trait is relabelled to match
		the Alpha Genes name, and a shared ToughSinews exclusion tag is put on the B&amp;S gene and the large body frames
		so a pawn cannot stack them.
		This folder only loads when B&amp;S - Genes &amp; More is active (see loadFolders.xml); Alpha Genes is gated inside.
		The mod gate sits on an <li> inside a sequence, not on the <Operation> itself: RimWorld reads
		MayRequire only on list elements, so an <Operation MayRequire="..."> node loads and applies
		unconditionally.

		Verified against the current 1.6 releases, with two things worth knowing:
		- AG_ToughSinews itself carries no exclusionTags upstream, so as written the tag only binds the Big and Small
		genes to each other. Nothing stops a pawn taking BS_GiantWeaponWielder and AG_ToughSinews together. Giving
		the Alpha Genes gene the same tag would be the fix, but that is a behaviour change, so it is left alone.
		- OgreFrame has no exclusionTags node, so the multi-def add skips it. The other four frames get the tag.
		Split by category into the MMMM Convergence sub-mods: this copy holds only the Genetics ops (genes and xenotypes).
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sarg.alphagenes">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/GeneDef[defName="BS_GiantWeaponWielder"]</xpath>
						<value>
							<exclusionTags>
								<li>ToughSinews</li>
							</exclusionTags>
						</value>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/GeneDef[defName="JotunFrame" or defName="OgreFrame" or defName="GreatOgreFrame" or defName="TitanFrame" or defName="BS_EndlessGrowth"]/exclusionTags</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>ToughSinews</li>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

	<!--
		Cherry Picker note: the astrogene entry is not dead weight. Alpha Genes defines no _Astrogene defs in XML at
		all, one per gene is built at runtime by AlphaGenes.dll, so the def exists in game even though grepping the
		mod's files finds nothing. An earlier comment in this project claimed otherwise; it was wrong.
		The list itself, MMMM_ConvergenceGenetics_CherryPicker_Basics, belongs to this mod, and the matching revive entries are
		in 1.6/Defs/CherryPicker.xml.
		Fix 2026-10-08: the retired gene is now swapped for BS_GiantWeaponWielder in every xenotype that carries it (dropped
		where the xenotype already has it). Before, Alpha Genes Integrated's Neanderthal lost tough sinews to Cherry Picker with
		nothing in its place. This folds in the standalone "Big and Small - Alpha Genes Integrated" mod (DanZinagri.BSAGI),
		which did the same for the Neanderthal only; About.xml marks it incompatible, since both would add the gene.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationSequence" MayRequire="sarg.alphagenes">
				<operations>
					<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[genes/li[text()="BS_GiantWeaponWielder"]]/genes/li[text()="AG_ToughSinews"]</xpath>
						<match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
							<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[genes/li[text()="BS_GiantWeaponWielder"]]/genes/li[text()="AG_ToughSinews"]</xpath>
						</match>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
						<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef/genes/li[text()="AG_ToughSinews"]</xpath>
						<match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
							<xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef/genes/li[text()="AG_ToughSinews"]</xpath>
							<value>
								<li>BS_GiantWeaponWielder</li>
							</value>
						</match>
					</li>
					<li Class="PatchOperationAdd">
						<xpath>Defs/CherryPicker.DefList[defName="MMMM_ConvergenceGenetics_CherryPicker_Basics"]/defs</xpath>
						<value>
							<li>GeneDef/AG_ToughSinews</li>
							<li>GeneDef/AG_ToughSinews_Astrogene</li>
						</value>
					</li>
				</operations>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
